WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.768
When callers need to react differently to
policy denial and evaluation failure,

2
00:00:04.848 --> 00:00:06.543
model the outcomes explicitly.

3
00:00:06.623 --> 00:00:08.758
A discriminated union with allow, deny,

4
00:00:08.838 --> 00:00:13.043
and indeterminate variants gives each
state a name and prevents undefined from

5
00:00:13.123 --> 00:00:15.320
becoming an undocumented fourth result.

6
00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.723
The protected branch should test for
allow,

7
00:00:17.803 --> 00:00:20.063
not merely test that the result is not
deny.

8
00:00:20.143 --> 00:00:23.156
An enforcement function can switch on the
decision kind.

9
00:00:23.236 --> 00:00:24.554
Allow returns normally.

10
00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:27.458
Deny throws a policy-specific
authorization error.

11
00:00:27.538 --> 00:00:31.681
Indeterminate throws an availability or
evaluation error while preserving a

12
00:00:31.761 --> 00:00:33.456
sanitized cause for telemetry.

13
00:00:33.536 --> 00:00:38.119
An exhaustive switch helps the compiler
identify unhandled variants when developers

14
00:00:38.199 --> 00:00:39.642
extend the internal union.

15
00:00:39.722 --> 00:00:43.928
This improves consistency without making
the type itself a security boundary.

16
00:00:44.008 --> 00:00:48.025
Decision metadata can carry an evaluation
identifier or policy version for

17
00:00:48.105 --> 00:00:51.809
diagnostics, but clients should not
receive sensitive rule details.

18
00:00:51.889 --> 00:00:54.274
External policy responses are runtime
data.

19
00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.928
Validate their shape, allowed decision
values,

20
00:00:57.008 --> 00:01:00.084
resource and action binding, timestamps
where relevant,

21
00:01:00.164 --> 00:01:04.809
and any integrity or transport guarantees
before constructing the internal decision.

22
00:01:04.889 --> 00:01:09.094
A TypeScript assertion does not prove that
a remote response matches the union.

23
00:01:09.174 --> 00:01:11.685
Unknown values, missing fields, parse
errors,

24
00:01:11.765 --> 00:01:15.657
and mismatched request identifiers remain
indeterminate, never allow.

25
00:01:15.737 --> 00:01:20.319
Avoid boolean or nullable expressions
whose permissive meaning depends on coercion.

26
00:01:20.399 --> 00:01:23.224
Result not equal to false accepts
undefined and null.

27
00:01:23.304 --> 00:01:27.196
Permission result coalesced with true
converts absence into authority.

28
00:01:27.276 --> 00:01:31.544
Catching an exception and returning true
converts infrastructure failure into

29
00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.064
access.

30
00:01:32.144 --> 00:01:36.224
A concise Boolean can still be safe when
its contract is total over valid local

31
00:01:36.304 --> 00:01:38.689
inputs and thrown failures block the
caller.

32
00:01:38.769 --> 00:01:42.787
The essential invariant is independent of
syntax: exactly one recognized,

33
00:01:42.867 --> 00:01:45.189
trusted outcome authorizes the operation,

34
00:01:45.269 --> 00:01:47.780
and every other outcome leaves it
unperformed.
